ubs, 5 of Spades, Ace of Spades. This gives us a flush draw (four spades total) and a gutshot straight draw (needing a Queen to make 10-J-Q-K-A). We have 12 outs (9 spades + 3 non-spade Queens) to make a very strong hand on the river. The opponent has checked the Pre-flop and Flop, showing passivity and likely weakness, but currently, we only have Jack-high.\n\nReason: Checking is the optimal play here to realize our equity for free. While a semi-bluff bet could be argued to capitalize on the opponent's weakness, checking guarantees we see the River card without risking chips while we are likely behind in current hand rank. If we hit our flush or straight on the River, we can value bet then.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
