his gives me 10-high with no pair. While I have two overcards to the board, I have no immediate straight or flush draws (only a runner-runner backdoor flush potential). The board texture (2-3-4) is very coordinated and likely hits the opponent's checking range (straights, sets, or two pair).\n\nReason: The opponent has bet 209 chips. Calling with just 10-high and very low equity is a losing play in the long run. Since I am currently leading the overall match (cumulative score +150), the best strategy is to play tight and minimize losses in small pots where I have a distinct disadvantage. Folding preserves my chip stack and lead.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
